+# Instruction observation
+
+Adapter-layer owner of shared instruction file observers and reference-counted leases. The registry normalizes selection and environment identity. The existing context resolver, project-root discovery and user-home selection are injected; this module does not duplicate instruction selection or parsing.
+
+Initialization binds watchers before resolving the initial snapshot. Failure closes all bound handles and removes the pending registry entry. Refreshes serialize; only live observers publish results. Snapshot identity includes all returned metadata (including original size behind a truncated prefix). Every asynchronous snapshot read rechecks its lease after awaits; disposed leases return undefined, even when another lease keeps the observer alive. Last release closes handles and debounce timer, evicts the registry entry, and prevents late publication. Dispose is idempotent.
+
+Native events debounce for 100 ms; missing candidates anchor to an existing ancestor. Watch failures and symlink indirection use request-boundary fingerprint fallback. No persistence, replay, network or UI delivery is introduced.
